+    "caa9_key_findings_detailed": "Four factors captured distributed GMV patterns. PW2 correlated with illness duration (r = -0.283, FDR p = 0.035) and age of onset (r = -0.336, FDR p = 0.020); NW1 and NW2 correlated with Y-BOCS (r = 0.242, FDR p = 0.049; r = 0.266, FDR p = 0.035). Female vs male: lower PW2 (t = -2.303, d = -0.466) and higher NW2 (t = 2.319, d = 0.469), FDR p = 0.047. Group t-test (age/sex/TIV covariates) showed no significant GMV differences (FDR < 0.05). Group-level differences explained by factors (R^2 = 0.700, p < 0.001). LOOCV predicted factor compositions with high R^2 (PW1 0.862; PW2 0.903; NW1 0.735; NW2 0.806; all permutation p < 0.001). Clustering yielded two subtypes; subtype 1 showed increased GMV and subtype 2 decreased GMV vs HCs (SPM12, FDR < 0.05, cluster > 100 voxels).",
